# Citation metadata for Jura Trace. GitHub shows a "Cite this repository"
# button from this file, and Zenodo reads it when it archives a release.
# At each release, change version and date-released (see
# docs/release/mac-release-runbook.md, after publishing).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Jura Trace in research or reporting, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Jura Trace"
abstract: >-
  Jura Trace is a free, open-source desktop application for checking images.
  It reads and adds C2PA Content Credentials, runs image forensic checks
  (error level analysis, noise, copy-move, JPEG ghost and others) and looks
  for signs of AI generation. All checks run on the user's own computer.
  It includes a command-line client and a local REST API.
authors:
  - given-names: Paul
    family-names: Griffiths
    affiliation: "Jura Labs CIC"
  - name: "Jura Labs CIC"
    website: "https://juralabs.org"
version: "1.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-20"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
url: "https://juralabs.org/jura-trace"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jura-Labs/jura-trace-dev"
repository-artifact: "https://github.com/Jura-Labs/jura-trace/releases"
keywords:
  - C2PA
  - Content Credentials
  - image forensics
  - provenance
  - AI-generated images
  - media verification
  - OSINT
